## I-06 — critical path

I-06 requires real isolated staging, not just documentation or local ASGI tests. Plan and later gather evidence for:

- separate staging DB/roles, web identity, Discord app/guild and credentials;
- loopback app behind the accepted proxy boundary;
- synthetic/anonymized data only, never a production backup;
- environment markers and fail-closed cross-environment validation;
- health, kill switch, startup refusal and monitoring;
- TC-LIM-02, browser half of TC-SEC-07, TC-OPS-01…05 and TC-PERF-01…03;
- browser OAuth/member/Council/import flows with Peter-approved staging identities;
- representative 64 MiB refusal, real-shape synthetic load and 32-Actor-class preview/apply measurements;
- `/healthz` and status responsiveness during work;
- worker restart, lease expiry, lost response and recovery; and
- backup, restore, rollback and rerun evidence.

Record exact timestamps, versions, environment identity, commands and outputs without secrets or unnecessary identity data. Do not close I-06 on undeployed configuration, local tests or written procedures.

## A-05 — Peter-participated host ceremony

On the intended staging/target host, with Peter's explicit authorization and participation:

- establish the protected Server Administrator account through supported host-local tooling;
- enroll at least two independent WebAuthn/passkey credentials;
- prove retirement below two credentials is refused;
- prove startup and `/healthz` readiness behavior;
- exercise emergency login during simulated Discord unavailability;
