## R-23 — accessibility residual

P3.4 automation passed, but TC-UI-01/02, TC-UI-08 and TC-UI-09 remain Not Run. In isolated staging cover:

- keyboard-only operation, no traps, visible/logical focus and skip links;
- semantics, headings, labels, descriptions and tables;
- denied, empty, loading, stale, validation and error states;
- HTMX-enhanced and JavaScript-disabled paths;
- 320/768/1280 viewports and 200% zoom/reflow;
- real-engine contrast and reduced motion; and
- documented screen-reader traversal when qualified capacity exists.

Record browser, OS, viewport, zoom, AT and versions. Screenshots use synthetic data only. If real-device or screen-reader review remains unavailable, retain Not Run and R-23 and state the production-readiness consequence.

## A-06 and representative operation

Measure PostgreSQL as the job-queue and cross-process-limiter substrate under representative staging conditions:

- preview/apply duration;
- worker peak RSS against the 1 GiB guard;
- portal health/status responsiveness;
- DB pool behavior;
- cross-process limiter behavior;
- lease heartbeat/commit-fence behavior; and
- recovery after worker interruption/lease expiry.

Use realistically shaped, bounded synthetic data—never real Actor payloads.

## Integration/security matrix

Map every Phase 3 acceptance/mandatory-test row to exact test node IDs, staging procedure IDs, outputs and status. Exercise at least:

- unauthenticated, non-member, member, Council, Administrator, combined and break-glass boundaries;
- membership/role revocation and session rotation/revocation;
- stable role IDs; object/job/character substitution denial;
- CSRF, Origin, Host, CORS, cookies and safe redirects;
- body/file limits, content type and malicious filenames;
- escaping of Actor, warning, username/global-name and audit content;
- safe correlation UUID and refusal/error bodies;
- import staleness, idempotency, double-click and two-browser concurrency;
- append-only audit and restricted-role mutation denial;
- absence of character-game-state correction routes;
- CSP/security headers on normal and early/error responses;
- no-JS essential workflows; and
- asset integrity, cache policy and traversal refusal.

Security, authorization, identity, atomicity, data-integrity, recovery or reliability findings are blocking. Material coverage, maintenance, performance or operational weaknesses are important. Route frontend-only findings to Gemini; cross-contract changes require explicit review and Peter's decision.

